[Music]  this morning on the dish a chef the  james beard foundation called the  darling of raleigh north carolina ashley  christensen was born and raised in the  state and grew up in a food loving  family but she didn't know she'd make  cooking her career until her first  culinary job at age 21. since then she's  opened six acclaimed restaurants and  with her wife and business partner is  co-author of two cookbooks including  their latest it's always freezer season  jamie wax sat down with them to talk  about that unusual theme and a wedding  to remember  after working in the kitchens of some of  the world's finest chefs  this is where chef ashley christensen's  own vision first became fully realized  the reimagining of a beloved downtown  diner called pools in the place she  loves most raleigh north carolina  actually when i look around this space  it's amazing to me  what you did to elevate  a southern diner but also what you did  to preserve the integrity of it i think  of it less as elevating and more of  celebrating celebrating the bones of  this place and its history  and i've said it over and over again  about this set of walls just that there  are so many great ghosts here and so  many  long-standing relationships with this  place long before i ever arrived  christensen's love of long-standing  relationships is evident in her six  incredibly diverse raleigh  establishments from beasley's chicken  and honey to poolside pies the  neapolitan inspired gourmet pizza joint  with a huge wood-fired oven as its  centerpiece  and a clever swimming pool theme  throughout the idea of playing off of  the name pools next door  and calling it poolside and pools of  course is spelled p-o-o-l-e  no matter how different the menu each of  her restaurants reflects the care  comfort and community that are central  to ashley christensen's cooking values  shared by her wife and culinary partner  caitlin golan i grew up in los angeles  in a family that loved food the adults  would just spend like several hours in  the kitchen the labor of food was never  it never felt like work it was always  part of the the time together the  fellowship together my background really  begins with my parents and and their  love for food as non-professional cooks  as home cooks the dna of christensen's  cooking comes from both parents her  mother traveled as an air force brat and  her father was a truck driver who came  home from every trip excited to share  the new recipes he had experienced on  his travels dad would come home and the  way that he would share with us to make  up for time he was away was to cook  dishes  that  he experienced on the red  food has always brought ashley and kate  together not only in life but also in  business their unique new cookbook it's  always freezer season is their latest  collaboration this book was so fun to  write because there were so many stories  and relationships that we got to pay  homage to  we love the food in this book  we're not sick of it yet the idea of  this book is to treat the freezer more  like a pantry a perfect concept for a  newly prolific crop of pandemic home  cooks  i love that you call the freezer the  most underutilized appliance in the  kitchen which is is really true right  yeah i mean for  us the freezer took on much more of a  preservation aspect than a simply a  chilling device which is i think sort of  where you start right but really what it  is in our minds is this storage space  for preserving the life of food that we  have either already made or that we you  know want to make and from their freezer  come global recipes with a southern  flair that include carnitas cornbread  panzanella with watermelon a creamy  citrusy salty dog pie and mac and cheese  with a twist pimento cheese something  most southerners know well i have to say  this custard style mac and cheese with  little hit of pimento cheese in it is  absolutely unbelievable awesome so  delicious awesome my mother will be so  excited  you know when people talk about pimento  cheese i think they think of these  store-bought tubs of something that's  very sort of gelatinous and  yeah slimy  which tastes good on its own but it's  nothing like this my pimento cheese is  inspired by my great godmother who was  from chillicothe ohio and made a very  different pimento cheese than i had ever  eaten in the south  and um so this is meant to be the  pimento cheese for people who did not  know they liked pimento peas to  the two have become a true north  carolina power couple in early 2020 the  pair wed in an elaborate but deeply  personal ceremony the two of you had the  coolest wedding i've ever seen in my  life we have some really beautiful  friendships with local musicians who  have gone into the  national world and done really fun  things and sharing their energy the  wedding was not only covered by vogue  magazine but also featured carolina  music royalty like justin vernon of  bonavere and another special guest bruce  bruce hornsby  total surprise and she like almost fell  over and as soon as i saw him i don't  know if i've ever been so speechless but  there was someone there who meant even  more than all the celebrities  her father i lost my father at the  beginning of this year but he has been  such a  always a huge part of inspiring both my  confidence and and my love for food you  named your bar for your father yeah so  my dad's uh nickname is fox and we have  a bar called fox that focus on the  personal has garnered christensen  multiple james beard awards as well as a  reputation as a champion for women in  every level of the restaurant industry  it also might be why even though ashley  christensen has all the world to choose  from she chooses to bloom where she's  planted you keep six excellent places in  a sound that you love  and just keep getting better well at  some point we realized that this this  should be about  not needing more spaces or places but  making sure that each of those evolve  and not viewing change as failure  but  exciting evolution  for cbs this morning saturday jamie wax  raleigh  okay the pimento mac and cheese is  officially now  on the menu for this weekend i think  right oh my gosh i was the lone person  eating pimento cheese sandwiches in  south carolina  because that's all i could eat and i  just love that it's in mac and mac and  cheese good wow raleigh is such a great  food city too yeah her restaurants i  mean all of those spaces look amazing i  love her i love everything about it both  of them and her wedding

